The engenty figures — the one-eyed characters of engenty, in every kind and rendering, with
their shapes, colours, eyes and accessories — are licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

You may use, copy, change and share them, commercially too, free of charge and without
royalties, as long as you give credit, for example:

    engenty figures © Thru The Heart Creative GmbH - Matthias Platzer, CC BY 4.0, engenty.ai

These files describe what the figures look like and are under CC BY 4.0:

- apps/web/src/engenty/engenty.tsx, colors.ts, forms.ts, helmet.tsx, logo.tsx,
  goose-helmet-fit.ts, assets/goose-helmet.bin, assets/goose-helmet-livery.webp
- apps/runtime/src/services/engenty-shapes.ts, plugin/hooks/engenty.ts
- assets/engenty/: every flat figure as a 512 px PNG, plain and, for round, drop, dome, flame,
  oval, sprout and tower, with the helmet
- apps/web/public/favicon.svg, apps/web/public/icons/, apps/docs/public/favicon.svg
- docs/assets/engenty.svg

The figures are under CC BY 4.0 wherever else they appear in this repository too: in the
screenshots docs/assets/setup.png, studio.png and wizard.png, and as the pixel engenty that
apps/web/public/install.sh draws. The rest of those files is under the Functional Source License.

The code that renders, animates and deforms the figures (the fur and jelly renderers and
their shaders, the helmet's geometry and shaders, gaze and motion) stays under the Functional
Source License (LICENSE).

